      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Heap is a binary Tree which is actually a complete Binary Tree .\n\n2. In heap parent and child has a special relation .\n\n3. The realtion is that if Heap is MAX heap then parent Node is\nalways greater than its both child nodes .\n\n4. If Heap is MIN heap then parent node is always smaller than its\nboth child nodes .",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Heap is a binary Tree which is actually a complete Binary Tree .\n\n2. In heap parent and child has a special relation .\n\n3. The realtion is that if Heap is MAX heap then parent Node is always greater than its both child nodes .\n\n4. If Heap is MIN heap then parent node is always smaller than its both child nodes .",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
